1
00:00:00,267 --> 00:00:01,900
Pellet or briquette.

2
00:00:01,900 --> 00:00:03,933
Both are pressed biomass,

3
00:00:03,933 --> 00:00:05,000
but they are

4
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:07,100
not the same product.

5
00:00:07,333 --> 00:00:08,733
Pellets are small,

6
00:00:08,733 --> 00:00:09,900
about the size

7
00:00:09,900 --> 00:00:11,300
of a pencil stub.

8
00:00:11,300 --> 00:00:14,300
They flow easily and feed automatically,

9
00:00:14,300 --> 00:00:16,300
which is why power plants

10
00:00:16,300 --> 00:00:19,600
co-firing biomass mostly ask for pellets.

11
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:21,000
Briquettes are bigger,

12
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:22,100
like short logs.

13
00:00:22,100 --> 00:00:24,667
They are popular with industrial boilers,

14
00:00:24,667 --> 00:00:26,567
brick kilns and factories.

15
00:00:26,567 --> 00:00:28,200
Pellets need finer,

16
00:00:28,200 --> 00:00:31,433
drier raw material and more processing,

17
00:00:31,433 --> 00:00:33,000
so a pellet plant

18
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:35,233
costs more to set up.

19
00:00:35,400 --> 00:00:37,500
Briquette machines are simpler,

20
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:38,667
which makes them

21
00:00:38,667 --> 00:00:40,767
an easier place to start.

22
00:00:40,867 --> 00:00:42,967
So which one should you make?

23
00:00:42,967 --> 00:00:45,367
It depends on two things.

24
00:00:45,367 --> 00:00:47,867
The raw material you have,

25
00:00:47,867 --> 00:00:50,867
and who is buying near you.

26
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Pellet makers,

27
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:53,200
briquette makers,

28
00:00:53,200 --> 00:00:55,000
and the buyers for both.

29
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:57,867
IndiaBiomass is bringing them together.
